# Fast local feedback on formatting, the highest-frequency CI failure in a
# formatter-enforced repo. CI's `lint-format` job is still the actual gate:
# this hook only runs for contributors who ran `npm ci` (which runs `prepare`),
# is skippable with `--no-verify`, and never runs for edits made through the
# GitHub web UI. Same reasoning as the commit-msg hook next to this file.
#
# Runs the biome pinned in package-lock.json rather than whatever an editor
# integration happens to provide, so a broken or missing IDE plugin cannot let
# a misformatted file through.
#
# Check-only, deliberately not `--write`: git has already snapshotted the index
# by the time a pre-commit hook runs, so a fix written here would not be part
# of the commit unless the hook re-staged it, and re-staging silently sweeps in
# hunks that `git add -p` deliberately left out. Report and stop instead; the
# fix is `npm run lint:fix`.
#
# `--staged` limits the check to files with staged changes, so a one-file
# commit is never blocked by an unrelated problem elsewhere in the tree.
#
# `--no-errors-on-unmatched`: a commit that stages only files biome does not
# handle (LICENSE, an .svg, an .md) checks zero files, which biome treats as an
# error without this flag, blocking a perfectly good commit.
npx --no -- biome check --staged --no-errors-on-unmatched
